From ff695adf3034475899f0c239d838c5c773d21717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:19:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Bug XXXXXXX - Add a pref to keep security key requests
 off the credential portal. r?mfarrell

With security.webauthn.use-xdg-desktop-portal enabled, every WebAuthn
request goes to the credential portal. Add
security.webauthn.use-xdg-desktop-portal.security-keys (default true, so
nothing changes by default). When it is false, requests meant for a
security key stay on authenticator-rs, and the portal only sees requests
that a platform or hybrid authenticator can serve.

A registration is meant for a security key when its hints say so, or
when it has no deciding hint and asks for a cross-platform authenticator.
An assertion is when its hints say so, or when every allowed credential
lists only security key transports. An explicit "platform" registration,
a discoverable credential request and a credential without transports
all go to the portal.

The classification lives in WebAuthnUtil so it can be tested without a
portal.
